Read remap rules from ``<file>``.

Each non-empty line in the file is one rule in either format:

| ``pattern=replacement``
| ``pattern replacement``

Lines beginning with ``#`` and blank lines are ignored. Inline ``#`` comments
are also supported.

Rules from this file are appended to the same ordered remap list used by
:option:`--remap-inputs`.

Rules are evaluated in command-line order; the first matching rule wins. The
pattern supports wildcard matching. For example, ``remap.txt`` can contain:

| ``foo.o=bar.o``
| ``*foo.o=build/alt/bar.o``

When used with ``--reproduce``, the remap file is copied into the reproduce
archive and the generated ``response.txt`` refers to the captured replacement
paths. This allows the extracted archive to be replayed without access to the
original remap file or the original input paths.
